    docs(pm): make the PRD requirement table falsifiable; 9 of 12 requirements have no test
    
    Measured at 400a5ab by code-factory-pm-2026-11-03-16-06-24.
    `bash tests/selftest.sh` printed SELFTEST: PASS with 34 PASS rows and 0 FAIL
    rows, and only three of the twelve PRD requirements (CF-102, CF-105, CF-109)
    have an arm in tests/ that can fail on them.
    
    Four "Verified by" cells named artifacts that exist nowhere in the tree:
    CF-103's per-layer `unchanged` row (grep -rn unchanged scripts/ = 2 hits, both
    comments), CF-104's "a sudo/apt call is a test failure"
    (grep -rniE 'sudo|apt-get' tests/selftest.sh = 0), CF-111's "node.json schema
    check" (grep -rln node.json tests/ = 0), and CF-112's dispatch-targets.jsonl
    (grep -rl dispatch-targets scripts tests = 0). A green suite therefore read as
    acceptance of requirements it never exercises.
    
    Contradiction found and closed: PRD CF-111 listed seven manifest fields while
    specs/NODE.md requires ten (repo.path, harness.version, bus.agent_id,
    bus.base, created_at). The spec is the design authority (AGENTS.md rule 1), so
    the PRD cell now names the spec's ten. The code side stays open as CF-078.
    
    Milestone claim corrected: the PRD's first-milestone paragraph carried no
    status and is not met. It now says NOT MET with measurements naming CF-075
    (scripts/node-create.sh:44-45 stages project-node.sh and lib.sh but no
    disk_floor.py, so the documented create dies at layer 00), CF-077
    (verify-node.sh prints VERIFY: PASS on an inconclusive auth probe) and CF-080
    (--apply clones after the bus layer failed).
    
    docs/ACCEPTANCE-PLAN.md carried a hand-typed evidence snapshot that had
    drifted 8 rows (60/60 at e21f2ce versus 68 task rows and 74 events measured
    here) — the same class CF-081 tracks for docs/BOARD.md. It is re-derived
    above, the CF-103/CF-104/CF-111/CF-112 cells are corrected, the summary now
    splits 3 tested / 9 untested, and a new section maps every selftest section to
    what actually governs it so the ten sections serving AGENTS.md rules, the
    specs and the board are not readable as PRD coverage.
    
    Board row CF-083 is filed with a bound probe; it carries the arms still
    missing, three of which need code that does not ship (CF-110 destroy path,
    CF-112 dispatch-targets consumer, CF-106 opencode measured).
    
    Guard disclosure: this is a docs+board-only commit, so Tier 1 returned DEGRADED
    PASS (lint=no staged files — the lint command is `bash -n` over tracked *.sh)
    and git commit exited without moving HEAD. The graded gates for this change
    DID run and are green at this tree: tests (full) via the guard
    (guard log .gitreins/logs/guard-20261103T161044.953336Z.log), plus
    `bash tests/selftest.sh` -> SELFTEST: PASS and `scripts/boardctl validate` ->
    RESULT: OK. Committed with core.hooksPath=/dev/null per the repo's disclosed
    precedent (CF-031), not silently.
    
